-- Round 324 — product tag backfill for `releases.tags` (PRJ/PUB
-- categories + freeform), from the team's CATALOG CSV ("TRACKING_FULL_
-- CATALOG_0809 - TRACKING - FULL CATALOG"), matched by UPC. Per explicit
-- request ("the CATALOG has the product tag backfill ... let's do some
-- import"). Cannot be run against the live database from here (no
-- credentials) — review before running.
--
-- Idempotent and non-destructive: every write is COALESCE/NOT-EXISTS
-- guarded — a release that already has its own PRJ_ or PUB_ tag keeps it
-- untouched (this only FILLS a release that has none), and a freeform tag
-- is only appended if not already present. Safe to run more than once,
-- and safe to run before or after add-round324-label-catalog-import.sql
-- (they touch different tables/columns).
--
-- Source data: 24940 distinct UPCs across the catalog (111,517 track
-- rows). Split into 9 independent chunks of up to 3000 UPCs each below —
-- each chunk is its own self-contained, idempotent UPDATE, so if one
-- times out or errors, only that chunk needs re-running.
--
-- Value mapping used (per explicit decisions this round):
--   Tag PRJ: 'PRJ_LICENSE' -> PRJ_LICENSED (spelling fix), 'End Contract'
--     -> PRJ_END, PRJ_INHOUSE/PRJ_OWNED/PRJ_UNKNOWN unchanged.
--   TAG PUB: PUB_VCPMC/PUB_AUTHOR/PUB_VIEENT/PUB_OWNER unchanged (already
--     matched this app's PUB_ vocabulary exactly, no mapping needed).
--   5 non-PRJ freeform values found mixed into the Tag PRJ column —
--     RELAXING, Nhạc Hoa Lời Việt, SOUNDTRACK, PHONK, nhạc ngoại — are
--     NOT mapped to any PRJ_ code (they aren't project-rights-type
--     values). Per explicit decision ("add them as normal tag but don't
--     code them in, they are discontinued"), they're imported as plain
--     freeform release tags instead — same freeform tag mechanism the
--     unified Tags row already supports (lib/releaseTags.js), just
--     seeded here rather than typed in by hand. "Discontinued" per that
--     same decision — nothing else in this SQL treats them specially,
--     but they're flagged here in case anyone later wants to clean them
--     off releases rather than keep them as tags.
--
-- Per-UPC conflicts (2+ DIFFERENT real PRJ_ or PUB_ codes recorded across
-- that UPC's own track rows, before any of the mapping above) are NOT
-- resolved automatically — that field is left blank for that UPC below
-- (freeform tags, if any, still get applied). 197 such conflicts found:
